<h2 id="planned">Planned</h2>
<note>Planned: not in the compiler yet. Each name below is described in the specification and is an error today (BYN2001 for an unknown namespace, BYN2003 for an unknown member).</note>
<ul>
<li><code>Fs</code>, <code>Env</code>, <code>Path</code> and <code>Target</code>: file-system, environment-variable, path and build-target namespaces. The specification gives <code>Path.join(rest parts)</code> for joining path segments. Until they exist, use <code>Io</code> for files, the <code>args</code> parameter of <code>main</code> for arguments, and plain strings for paths.</li>
<li>Numeric members: <code>abs</code>, <code>sqrt</code>, <code>floor</code>, <code>ceiling</code>, <code>rounded()</code>, <code>truncated()</code>, <code>clamped(from:, through:)</code>, <code>pow</code>, and the free functions <code>min</code> and <code>max</code> (specification section 16.2).</li>
<li>List and sequence queries: <code>first</code>, <code>last</code>, <code>contains</code>, <code>indexOf</code>, <code>any</code>, <code>all</code>, <code>where</code>, <code>select</code>, <code>sorted</code>, <code>reversed</code>, <code>prepend</code>, <code>insert</code>, <code>Set</code>, <code>Deque</code> (section 16).</li>
<li>Text beyond the string members above: full Unicode case folding, normalization, grapheme handling (section 16.4).</li>
<li><code>Event&lt;T&gt;</code> for in-process notification (section 16.1) and <code>std.db</code> (section 16.3).</li>
</ul>
<pre><code class="byn">let joined = Path.join(root, "orders", $"{id}.json")
let home = Env.get("HOME") ?? "/"
let first = xs.first ?? 0</code></pre>
